{
  "description": "Explicit Blender 5.2.2 behavior scenarios only. Known gaps require an activating Blender input and are checked against Blender at test time; inert cases are confirmed no-ops under their recorded condition. Cast scenarios use a factor 0 baseline (Blender and Potter both leave the box unchanged). cast_default sends the schema defaults only; on a size-2 box every vertex is equidistant from the origin, so the default auto-sized sphere is a Blender no-op there and the scenario checks that Potter's default evaluates to the same no-op. The default's active effect is covered by cast_defaults_and_limits_match_blender_on_uneven_and_zero_geometry.",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "edge_split_no_angle",
      "primitive": "box",
      "modifier": "edge_split",
      "baseline_params": {},
      "case_params": {
        "use_edge_angle": false
      },
      "expectation": "equal_active"
    },
    {
